,title,link,text,language,family
0,Heiltsuk dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heiltsuk_dialect,"December 29, 2025 - Heiltsuk (/ˈheɪltsək/, Híɫzaqv), also known as Bella Bella and Haihais, is a dialect of the North Wakashan (Kwakiutlan) language Heiltsuk-Oowekyala that is spoken by the Haihai (Xai'xais) and Bella Bella First Nations peoples of the Central Coast region of the Canadian province of British ...",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
1,Kwakwakaʼwakw music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwakwakaʼwakw_music,"April 29, 2026 - The Kwakwakaʼwakw are a collective of twenty-five nations of the Wakashan language family who altogether form part of a larger identity comprising the Indigenous Peoples of the Pacific Northwest Coast, located in what is known today as British Columbia, Canada.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
2,Kwakwakaʼwakw - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwakwakaʼwakw,"April 3, 2026 - The term became misapplied to mean ... whose language is a part of the Wakashan linguistic group, but whose language is not Kwakʼwala. These peoples, incorrectly known as the Northern Kwakiutl, were the Haisla, Wuikinuxv, and Heiltsuk....",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
3,Heiltsuk–Oowekyala language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heiltsuk–Oowekyala_language,"December 29, 2025 - Heiltsuk–Oowekyala is a Northern Wakashan (Kwakiutlan) language spoken in the Central Coast region of the Canadian province of British Columbia, spoken by the Wuikinuxv (Oweekeno) and Heiltsuk peoples. It has two dialects, Heiltsuk (Bella Bella) and Oowekyala (Wuikyala), which unlike other ...",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
4,Haisla people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haisla_people,"May 22, 2026 - It is a Northern Wakashan language spoken by several hundred people, and is geographically the northernmost Wakashan language. Its nearest Wakashan neighbour is Oowekyala. Haisla is related to the other North Wakashan languages of Wuikyala, Heiltsuk, and Kwak'wala.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
5,Haiɫzaqvla (Heiltsuk / Bella Bella),https://www.languagegeek.com/wakashan/hailhzaqvla.html,"It is currently used in Kitasoo and Bella Bella, with several modifications (shown at the Bella Bella Community School page). The main differences are shown below in the charts, with Rath’s orthography in parenthesis. It appears from the Heiltsuk Nation website, that this is the official standard.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
6,Heiltsuk Singing at Hakai - Go to Ep 8 www.wildarchaeology ...1319 Heiltsuk ceremonial songs - thebcreview.caHeiltsuk dialect - WikipediaOral history of early Chinook Jargon use for lying to enemies ...‘I can still hear their words’: the fight to save the Híɫzaqv ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8U_uFVMgTg,"Elroy White of Bella Bella on the Central Coast of B.C. sings a Heiltsuk ancestral song to the hosts of Wild Archaeology. Dec 12, 2021 · Kolstee’s thesis is that the ceremonial song repertoire of the Heiltsuk is made up of four distinct musical styles and that a four-part organization is ubiquitous in Heiltsuk musical patterning. It is one of the four Northern Wakashan languages, the others being Haisla (spoken in Kitimaat), Oowekyala (in Rivers Inlet), and Kwakwala (in Alert Bay, Port Hardy, and various settlements). 3 days ago · On pages 132 and 133 is Willy Gladstone’s narrative titled “War with th e ᵋwī′k!ēnoxᵘ“ (that’s the Oweekeno people, who have a Northern Wakashan language closely related to Heiltsuk/Bella Bella). Jan 21, 2025 · Centuries ago, the music of the Híɫzaqv language echoed across a territory of deep fjords, rugged islands, windswept beaches and thick forests. Where is Heiltsuk spoken? Heiltsuk is spoken in the villages of Bella Bella and Klemtu, both located on coastal islands in British Columbia not far from Bella Coola and Ocean Falls. It is one of the four Northern Wakashan languages, the others being Haisla (spoken in Kitimaat), Oowekyala (in Rivers Inlet), and Kwakwala (in Alert Bay, Port Hardy, and various settlements). How many vowels does Heiltsuk have? Heiltsuk has phonemic short, long, and glottalized vowels. There are mainly three vowel sounds in the Heiltsuk dialect /i, a, u/ which are written as ⟨i, a, u⟩, although nine other sounds are heard as allophones [ɨ, ɪ, ʊ, ɛ, ə, ɔ, æ, ʌ, ɑ]. Is Heiltsuk endangered? Heiltsuk is classified as Critically Endangered by the UNESCO Atlas of the World's Languages in Danger.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
7,1319 Heiltsuk ceremonial songs - thebcreview.ca,https://thebcreview.ca/2021/12/12/1319-turin-kolstee-heiltsuk/,"Dec 12, 2021 · Kolstee’s thesis is that the ceremonial song repertoire of the Heiltsuk is made up of four distinct musical styles and that a four-part organization is ubiquitous in Heiltsuk musical patterning.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
8,The Heiltsuk-Oweek'ala Language,https://www.ydli.org/langs/heiltsuk.htm,Heiltsuk is a Wakashan language.,Heiltsuk,Wakashan
9,Haíɫzaqvḷa / Heiltsuk Language – Languagegeek,https://languagegeek.com/lgwp/languages/wakashan-languages/haiɫzaqvḷa-heiltsuk-language/,"Heiltsuk (ISO 639-3 hei) is a northern Wakashan language spoken mid-way up the Pacific coast of British Columbia. The writing system presented here is based on the practical orthography as shown in Rath 1981. The current form is used in Kitasoo and Bella Bella, with several modifications.",Heiltsuk,Wakashan
